      ],
      "status": "not_affected",
      "justification": "component_not_present",
      "impact_statement": "The Minerva timing attack is in `ecdsa`, which reached ION only as a transitive dependency of python-jose. ION migrated to PyJWT, which pulls `cryptography` and no `ecdsa`, so the package is absent from the image."
    },
    {
      "vulnerability": {
        "name": "MAL-2026-4750"
      },
      "products": [
        {
          "@id": "pkg:docker/fubsxploitapps/ion@0.99.15"
        }
      ],
      "status": "not_affected",
      "justification": "component_not_present",
      "impact_statement": "The compromised artefact is the fastapi 0.136.3 wheel, whose metadata adds an undocumented dependency on a typo-squat package. ION pins fastapi >=0.136.1,<0.136.3, so the affected release is never resolved. ION also does not use the [standard] extra through which the typo-squat would have installed."
    },
    {
      "vulnerability": {
        "name": "CVE-2025-71176"
      },
      "products": [
        {
          "@id": "pkg:docker/fubsxploitapps/ion@0.99.15"
        }
      ],
      "status": "not_affected",
      "justification": "component_not_present",
      "impact_statement": "The /tmp race is in pytest, which is a dev extra. The runtime image installs only the resolved runtime venv, so pytest is not present in a shipped ION container."
    },
